---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="About Umi-Time">
  <div class="umi-region umi-pad">
    <main class="about">
      <section class="hero">
        <h1>About Umi‑Time</h1>
        <p>
          Umi‑Time expresses the 24‑hour UTC day as a smooth 360‑unit cycle.
          Every location on Earth shares the same umi value at the same moment,
          giving Umi‑Time a universal, continuous representation of the day.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>What Is Umi‑Time?</h2>
        <p>
          What changes from place to place is the orientation of the dial. The
          dial rotates according to longitude, placing Umi‑Time Noon at the top
          and Umi‑Time Midnight at the bottom for each observer. This rotation
          gives Umi‑Time its local interpretability without altering the
          underlying universal value.
        </p>
        <p>
          Umi‑Time builds directly on UTC, preserving its stability and
          precision while presenting the day in a form that is easier to read,
          compare, and reason about.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>Why Umi‑Time Exists</h2>
        <p>
          Civil time was built for regions, borders, and policies — not for a
          connected world. It fragments the day into zones, offsets, and
          seasonal rules that differ from place to place and change over time.
        </p>
        <p>
          UTC solved many of these problems by providing a single, stable
          reference for global coordination. Umi‑Time builds on that foundation,
          offering a clear, continuous representation of the UTC day that is
          intuitive for people and straightforward for systems.
        </p>
        <p>
          Developed by Daniel Brannon in 2026, Umi‑Time is designed to make our
          clocks universal and local at the same time.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <h2>What Makes Umi‑Time Different</h2>
        <p>Umi‑Time is:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Universal:</strong> one shared value for the entire world, derived
            directly from UTC.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Locally oriented:</strong> the dial rotates by longitude, giving
            each observer a meaningful view of the day.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Human‑friendly:</strong> the 360‑unit cycle is simple to visualize
            and compare.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Compatible:</strong> integrates cleanly with UTC and systems that
            already rely on it.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Umi‑Time is designed to provide a unified daily reference, offering a
          shared way to understand the day without the fragmentation of time
          zones or seasonal offsets.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>
</Base>
